Now I understand the crash path. The crash is a heap-buffer-overflow READ in `File::Write` called from `ComprDataIO::UnpWrite` called from `CmdExtract::UnstoreFile`. 

The issue is in `UnstoreFile`:
```cpp
void CmdExtract::UnstoreFile(ComprDataIO &DataIO,int64 DestUnpSize)
{
  Array<byte> Buffer(File::CopyBufferSize());
  while (1)
  {
    uint Code=DataIO.UnpRead(&Buffer[0],Buffer.Size());
    if (Code==0 || (int)Code==-1)
      break;
    Code=Code<DestUnpSize ? Code:(uint)DestUnpSize;
    DataIO.UnpWrite(&Buffer[0],Code);
    ...
```

The `Buffer` is allocated with `File::CopyBufferSize()`. Let me check what `UnpRead` does and what `CopyBufferSize` is. The issue is likely that `UnpRead` can return more data than the buffer size, or `DestUnpSize` can be larger than the buffer size, causing `UnpWrite` to read beyond the buffer.

Let me look at `UnpRead`:

